      "writtenOn": "2024-02-02T18:59:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was thinking of the threshold as a gate, so in the example of Brox I set it to 50ms (20Hz). So any time the AP or EC set the sample rate to 20Hz or below, this will kick in. I wanted to allow the flexibility of if the AP requested 5Hz we\u0027ll sleep 200ms, if 10Hz then 100ms, instead of using a compile time constant of 50ms even if we can sleep for 200ms.",
      "parentUuid": "8fe19e51_64f2bd00",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 205,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 206,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "57ee0cf77e3caa1353522ea7080df60366547983",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fa1a5021_fd077770",
        "filename": "common/motion_sense.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 206,
      "author": {
        "id": 1104704
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-02T19:40:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "But it breaks the case when we are in S3 and want to collect samples every 200ms. The |ec_rate| is  what will delay the scheduling.",
      "parentUuid": "71f06e18_a39c8df8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 205,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 206,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "57ee0cf77e3caa1353522ea7080df60366547983",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6375f8fb_57d732c3",
        "filename": "common/motion_sense.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 206,
      "author": {
        "id": 1333748
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-05T09:38:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think it does, here\u0027s the sample I ran:\n\n- Assuming a threshold of 50ms and an S3 ODR of 5Hz\n- Set the ODR to 5000mHz (200ms delay)\n- `enable` will be `false` since 1000000 / 5000 (200ms) is above the threshold of 50ms\n- call `enable_interrupt(sensor, false)` to turn off interrupts\n- `ec_rate \u003d 1000000000 / 5000 \u003d 200000` which gives us the 200ms sleep. If we used the threshold we would only sleep for 50ms.",
      "parentUuid": "fa1a5021_fd077770",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 205,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 206,
        "endChar": 38
      },
